  "verbalization": "Epi-actephilol A is shown to interact with multiple targets, including CX-1 and MOVP-3, which in turn target CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence suggests that Epi-actephilol A may exert its biological effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of CCRF-HSB-2. The final_score values indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism of action remains partially elucidated. The interaction with CX-1 and MOVP-3 implies that Epi-actephilol A may act through a complex network of targets, potentially involving multiple pathways. The presence of a direct interaction with CCRF-HSB-2 suggests that the compound may have a specific role in modulating the activity of this cell line, though further investigation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism of action and its relevance to the disease state.",
